@startuml checkin_surfaces
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' checkin_surfaces — v28.2 part 2: the knock, the tap, and the two walls
' that keep mood on the machine. Companion to checkin_gate (the WHEN).
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!include _style.puml

title Check-in part 2 — one tap to answer, two walls around the answer

component "CheckInService\n10-min timer · lastOffered\nin QSettings (per-device)" as svc
component "NotificationToast\nToastSpec + action row\n(the v28.0 seam's first consumer)" as toast
component "ChatPage::beginCheckIn\nC++ opener + 3 buttons\nall bubbles localOnly" as chat
database "AppData\nrecordMood (upsert)\nformat v12" as data
component "brief::dayBriefing\nOptions.includeMood\n<b>default false</b>" as brief
cloud "cloud seat" as cloud
component "local seat\n(loopback only —\nai::isLocal)" as local

svc --> toast : offer(title, body)\nmark lastOffered AT EMIT
toast --> chat : tap «Check in»\n→ showPage(6)
chat --> data : one tap = recordMood
data ..> brief : coarse level only

brief --> local : MOOD line rides\n(every route seat local)
brief -[#C25B54]-> cloud : <b>never</b> — mixed or remote\nroutes get silence

note bottom of chat
  §E.4 in part 2, satisfied by SUBTRACTION:
  no model is in the check-in loop at all —
  opener and acknowledgement are C++ citing
  evidence (§G.3). The model joins when
  per-role primaries exist.
end note

note bottom of svc
  Marked at EMIT, not at tap: a dismissed
  toast was still an ask. Marking at tap
  would re-knock at someone who already
  said "not now" with their thumb.
end note
@enduml
